{
  "task": "A - PRCC of dynamic model outputs (baseline scenario)",
  "method": "LHS (sensitivity.sample_lhs, n=2000, seed=20260816) over the 8 published parameter ranges; each sample propagated through the full ODE model (model.solve, t_span=(0,1095), daily output). PRCC = Marino et al. (2008): rank-transform inputs and output, regress each on the remaining 7 ranked inputs, Pearson correlation of residuals. p-values from a two-sided t-test with df = n - 2 - (k-1) = n - 9.",
  "temperature_handling": "b and sigma_v keep their temperature dependence; the sampled values act as level scalings relative to the 28 degC reference value (b_ref=0.214700 /day, sigma_v_ref=0.235217 /day = 1/4.2514 d). This avoids the constant-parameter substitution used in the static analysis.",
  "cumulative_metric": "cum_infected = 1 - Sh(1095)/Nh (proportion ever infected, attack-rate analogue). Cross-check (Eh+Ih+Rh)(1095)/Nh differs only by the imported cases injected directly into Ih; mean absolute difference = 7.82e-03.",
  "peak_definition": "peak_ih / peak_day from a 1096-point daily grid, then refined by a 3-point parabola around the argmax (needed to break the 1-day quantisation of peak_day in the rank transform). Peak value bias of the raw grid relative to a 1000-point grid is < 0.5%.",
